# The same placeholder under TotalRate, which is the shape where it means
# what it looks like.
#
# Without TotalRate the value of a rate function is multiplied by the rule's
# reactant match counts to get the propensity, so a count supplied by
# reactant_1() lands on the propensity twice.  With TotalRate the rate
# function states the whole propensity, so reactant_1()*kf() is exactly
# ordinary mass action at rate k, and RM emits no warning about it.
#
# Verified against NFsim on this model, 20 seeds each to t = 10000:
# RM 35.8, NFsim 37.7, against the 100*exp(-1) = 36.8 the law predicts.
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1e-4
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(s~0~1)
end molecule types
begin species
  A(s~0) 100
end species
begin observables
  Molecules Aoff A(s~0)
end observables
begin functions
  reactant_1()
  kf()=k
end functions
begin reaction rules
  A(s~0) -> A(s~1)  reactant_1()*kf() TotalRate
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
writeXML()
end actions
